  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n75%>50%,\n$$\n\nmore than half of Ethan's races were freestyle.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n0.4<0.5.\n$$\n\nSo, less than half of Lucas's races were freestyle.\n\n- Statement III is true. We can compare $75%$ and $0.4$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.4\\times 100=40%\n$$\n\nSince $75%>40%,$ Ethan had a **greater** percentage of freestyle races compared to Lucas.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
